DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  ssttrrccoollll() function compares the two strings _s_1 and _s_2.  It returns
       an integer less than, equal to, or greater than zero if  _s_1  is  found,
       respectively,  to  be  less than, to match, or be greater than _s_2.  The
       comparison is based on strings interpreted as appropriate for the  pro‐
       gram’s current locale for category LLCC__CCOOLLLLAATTEE.  (See sseettllooccaallee(3).)

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       The  ssttrrccoollll()  function  returns  an  integer  less than, equal to, or
       greater than zero if _s_1 is found, respectively, to  be  less  than,  to
       match,  or be greater than _s_2, when both are interpreted as appropriate
       for the current locale.

